From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:53:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] kk: allow LINEAR images as input attachments

Swapchains of zink and of the Gamescope WSI layer ask for
INPUT_ATTACHMENT usage. Through virglrenderer's emulated LINEAR DRM
modifier (Venus on macOS) the host checks that usage with LINEAR tiling;
KosmicKrisp refused it, so the guest WSI found no supported modifier and
vkCreateSwapchainKHR failed with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY (mangoapp,
X11 clients through gamescope).

Linear planes get a 2D texture plus a 2D array view for input
attachments ("kk: Create linear array textures as 2D plus a view"), so
only depth/stencil attachments stay unsupported with LINEAR tiling.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c | 13 +++++--------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
index 10562e0..278dc30 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image.c
@@ -274,16 +274,13 @@ kk_GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2(
        pImageFormatInfo->type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_3D)
       return VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 
-   /* TODO_KOSMICKRISP Linear images cannot be used as color attachments as long
-    * as input attachments are changed to arrays. Vulkan specifies that any
-    * image format supporting the color attachment feature also supports being
-    * used as an input attachment, and Metal disallows arrays for linear
-    * textures.
+   /* Linear (buffer-backed) textures are 2D only, input attachments are 2D
+    * arrays: a linear plane gets a 2D texture and a 2D array view of it (see
+    * kk_image_plane_create_texture), so linear images can be input attachments.
+    * Depth/stencil formats have no linear support in Metal.
     */
    if (pImageFormatInfo->tiling == VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR &&
-       (pImageFormatInfo->usage &
-        (VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT |
-         VK_IMAGE_USAGE_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_BIT)))
+       (pImageFormatInfo->usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_BIT))
       return VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 
    if (ycbcr_info && pImageFormatInfo->type != VK_IMAGE_TYPE_2D)
